+
+The user explicitly requested continuing this Arbor task autonomously without routine intervention, and the execution specification authorizes necessary engineering fixes and tests within the research budget. This is a coordinator interpretation of that continuing authority, not a new user approval. It does not change the cumulative 478-attempt / 100-GPU-hour limits, any bucket ceiling, protected reserves, scientific algorithm, target, validation/formal gate, or provider. Only the current Codex managed login may be used in later online Stage; Poe remains unused and its credentials are preserved.
+
+This document explicitly adds one narrowly bounded engineering recovery to the assistant-authored original N23 v1/v2 one-opportunity rule. It does not assert that rule allowed the failed attempt to be retried, conceal a second attempt under a new algorithm name, or reclassify the original attempt. Original v1/v2 protocols, plan, source, release, report and journal are immutable. Across the original opportunity and this exception there may be at most two N23 backend attempts total, of which only this one can run repaired code. There is no further backend recovery under this exception.
+
+## Exact eligibility
+
+The only eligible predecessor is `rdt-qd-ed-final-20260921T093925Z__n23_backend_preflight_v2__7ca117f9b7fb`, original source commit `77302aab40d6b059e85c8d1d8011ea36cb3d3856`, original plan SHA256 `44147944afdc773938d2a97ce564dc2fc9e184ac2cac2957df006d70489213d1`.
