+Bind and verify the root failure review `backend-failure-review-v1.json` SHA256 `95353cd515ca1e759e781d63108ecf03fcdea62372c7d1578159fe79a225c661`, all referenced report/plan/terminal bytes, and the exact reserved/dispatched/aborted ledger group. Require its error list exactly `RuntimeError:audit physical CUDA UUID differs or unavailable`, no arithmetic or synthetic batches, no task outcome, no Dev reservation across any N23 name, no live owner, and all old costs retained. A different error, real UUID mismatch evidence, arithmetic mismatch, partially evaluated corpus, unresolved attempt, or prior repair reservation cannot enter. The failed worker did not retain raw UUID; do not claim the live value was observed. Existing accounted GPU7 evidence and CPU reproduction support the representation defect only.
+
+## Code and scientific identity
+
+The executor first implements and CPU-tests strict UUID canonicalization: accept proper bare or GPU-prefixed UUID strings, preserve the raw observed value, compare canonical GPU-prefixed identities, reject missing/malformed/different UUID, and retain all CUDA mask/count/current-device gates. The worker receipt must verify canonical/raw consistency. The root must review and freeze the complete final source before any repaired GPU call.
+
+Changes from original source are limited to that identity compatibility fix, its tests, and the explicitly bounded repair admission/proof/source-manifest plumbing and this document. QD/ED implementation, candidate profiles, scoring arithmetic, batch order, corpus, float tolerances, Stage/perception/prompts, model/checkpoint, runtime dependency fingerprints, source data, simulator and all protected phase conditions must remain byte-identical. No general retry switch or relaxed arbitrary failure acceptance.
+
+Use fresh versioned repair plan/release/report paths and a new attempt with explicit `retry_of` pointing to the failed backend attempt. Require a root-owned hash-bound repair authority and source review in private state before dispatch. Do not overwrite any earlier final review, frozen plan, attempt or outcome.
+
+## One repaired backend worker
+
+One exclusive idle GPU7 worker, the same UUID/EGL/runtime and accounted health probe. Reserve and charge one existing recovery slot before dispatch, with 120 seconds plus 40 seconds cleanup. Preserve original 6.538148973020725 seconds as well. No budget increase; require whole remaining Dev ceiling, both originally planned Dev timeout recovery slots and validation/formal reserves to fit. No model load, provider call, environment reset, simulator step, reward learning or new data.
+
+Replay the exact unchanged original N21 task0 corpus (176 canonical batches / 2816 candidates from the original 2250 saved bundles) and the exact original two synthetic FP32/BF16 batches with identical arithmetic checks and wrong-bound rejection. Accept only full strict arithmetic proof, complete dtype/device/process identity and terminal cost evidence. An error, timeout, mismatch or missing evidence closes this repair; no tolerance tuning or second repair execution.
+
+## Conditional continuation
+
+Only a valid repaired proof with exactly matching final Dev source/runtime can unlock the original N23 v2 Dev matrix, unchanged four arms, tasks/seeds/order, scientific profiles, limits, narrow Codex-timeout recovery rules and promotion criteria. Include this engineering exception and both backend attempt references in Dev provenance. No N23 task outcomes exist before the repair. A failure does not scientifically reject N23 but leaves Dev closed. Protected validation and formal remain closed until their original genuine scientific gates.
+
+CPU preparation is authorized now. This document alone does not dispatch a worker: concrete root review, named failure proof, locked authority adoption, actual capacity and final frozen plan are all required.
